The null-check and validity test are folded into one short-circuit expression, removing the separate branch/return and the temporary pointer use so the compiler emits a tighter inlined sequence around the `GetField(8)` lookup.

```cpp
    FIT_BOOL IsFavoriteValid() const
    {
        const Field* field = GetField(8);
        return (FIT_NULL != field) && field->IsValueValid();
    }
```